  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); business-type from the proprietary funds statement Total column (p6), measure 'cash' (cash-basis statement), as in FY2023/FY2024. Governmental balance-sheet lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p3; totals equal the government-wide p1 governmental column). Governmental balances recorded as fund balances (beginning 940,123, ending 1,152,531, p4); cash fields not filled, as in later years (governmental cash printed only as separate lines: cash 789,724, county treasurer 1,873, CDs 313,288, restricted cash 47,646; see balance_sheet). Governmental: 940,123 + 276,932 - 297,524 + 233,000 = 1,152,531. Business-type: 1,125,995 + 768,058 - 465,220 - 233,000 = 1,195,833 (transfers in 20,000 Trash, out 253,000 Electric/Water/Sewer). Expenditures are printed by object with no function; function chosen from the fund columns (review). The only supplementary schedule (p7, all-funds budget to actual, receipts/disbursements include transfers 253,000) is combined, so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental (p4) and proprietary (p6) statements; the p7 schedule is not recorded. Business-type receipts total = operating 762,034 + nonoperating 6,024 (no single printed total). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
